your screen content (and optionally your microphone or camera) is captured. You are responsible for ensuring you have the right to record any content visible on your screen,
including content belonging to third parties,
confidential business information,
or other people's personal data.</p>
 </div><h3>How recording works technically</h3><p>VibeCam uses the browser's native <code>getDisplayMedia()</code> and <code>getUserMedia()</code> APIs. These are standard, permission-gated Web APIs. Your browser will always prompt you for explicit permission before any capture begins. We cannot capture your screen silently or without your active consent.</p>

<h3>What we capture</h3><ul><li><strong>Screen content:</strong>Exactly what you choose to share in the browser permission dialog (entire screen, a specific window, or a browser tab).</li><li><strong>System audio:</strong>Only on Chrome and Edge,
and only if you tick "Share system audio" in the browser's own permission prompt.</li>
 <li><strong>Microphone audio:</strong>Only if you toggle "Mic audio" on in VibeCam before recording.</li><li><strong>Camera:</strong>Only if you toggle "Camera bubble" on. This appears as a picture-in-picture overlay in your recording.</li></ul><h3>Where recordings are stored</h3><p><strong>Version 1 (local):</strong>Recordings are stored in your browser's <code>localStorage</code> or <code>IndexedDB</code> on your device. Nothing is sent to our servers unless you click Share.</p>
 <p><strong>Version 2 (cloud sharing):</strong>When you click Share,
the recording is uploaded to our cloud storage (Cloudflare R2) so it can be accessed via a shareable link. At this point the recording data leaves your device and is stored on our infrastructure.</p><h3>Access to your recordings</h3><p>Our staff do not routinely access the content of your recordings. We may access recording content only if: (a) required by a valid legal order;
(b) you report a specific recording to us for abuse review;
or (c) necessary to investigate a breach of our Terms of Service with your consent.</p><h3>Third-party content in recordings</h3><p>If your recording contains personal data of other individuals (e.g., you record a video call),
you become a data controller for that data under applicable privacy law. You must ensure you have a lawful basis to record and share that content.</p></div>< !-- 4 --><div class="section" id="s4"><div class="section-number">04</div><h2>How We Use Your Data</h2><p>We use the data we collect for the following purposes:</p><ul><li><strong>To operate the Service</strong>— storing,
